					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1019930&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609167909" alt="Anaxagoras" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1019930)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;" >Anaxagoras</a></span> <span class="odate time_1405835864 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Jul 2014 05:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2072212">
									

<p>It's not bad, but it reads more like a tale for the Tooth Fairies than an SCP in its own right. It also feels a bit nastier than follows naturally from the concept. I don't quite buy the teeth being all pseudo-enamel, nor the super-viral spread of them. I can buy an evil doctor, but I don't see him immediately jumping to murder with so little motivation.</p>

							</div>

								
					
